      <h2 style="font:600 var(--type-display-2)/1.08 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 40px;color:var(--color-forest);text-wrap:pretty">Questions we get</h2>
      
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:28px 40px">
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">Do you test with real student data?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">No. We use synthetic accounts and records. There is no testing benefit to real student data and considerable legal risk in touching it.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">Can you test our LTI integration?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Yes. LTI launches and OneRoster syncs are in scope and are a common source of role-assertion flaws between systems.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">How do you handle the role matrix?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">We provision an account for every distinct role and attempt every operation as each one, including unauthenticated. Education platforms usually have more roles than teams expect.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">Will your report satisfy a district security review?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">It provides the penetration testing evidence districts ask for, plus an attestation letter you can share directly with procurement.</p>
